### Did the Donald Trump administration roll back or weaken federal regulations designed to limit carbon emissions, such as the Clean Power Plan or vehicle fuel economy standards, and what was the projected impact of those rollbacks on emission levels?
Answer: Yes, the Trump administration weakened vehicle emissions standards by finalizing the Safer Affordable Fuel-Efficient (SAFE) Vehicles Rule, which increased carbon dioxide emissions standards for automakers by only 1.5% a year through model year 2026, compared to the 5% annual increase planned under the Obama administration. Critics projected that this rollback "will lead to nearly a billion additional metric tons of climate warming CO2 in the atmosphere."

